& [PreservedUserInstruction]
  + [verbatim] "take another 5-hour slice"
  + [continuity] continue after the native build and ArtifactReceipt lifecycle milestone rather than closing the broader shift
  + [selected_frontier] expose the completed authority chain through the smallest deterministic read-only machine protocol so Cantor and later tool adapters can inspect it

& [Purpose]
  + accept one bounded strict JSON request containing already-supplied native build lifecycle forms
  + replay those forms through the existing Slice5 and Slice6 validators in dependency order
  + return one compact deterministic JSON result identifying the deepest valid stage, exact identities, and any typed validation faults
  + make the authority-separated compiler lifecycle callable without creating a production runner

& [Request]
  + owns a complete candidate-to-artifact bundle and may optionally own an independent verification bundle
  + selects validate_artifact or validate_verification explicitly
  + carries trust public keys and signatures but never private signing material
  + rejects unknown fields, duplicate semantic identities, trailing JSON, oversized input, unsupported version, and incomplete optional stages

& [Validation]
  + replays seed, IR, candidate plan, native candidate projection, build plan, build capability, sandbox admission, approval, authorization, observation, attempt ledger, and ArtifactReceipt
  + verification mode additionally replays verifier plan, verifier observation, and verification receipt
  + reports valid only when every supplied form is exact and all required lineage agrees
  + preserves passed, failed, and unresolved verification dispositions as valid recorded outcomes rather than conflating validity with a passing artifact

& [Response]
  + identifies protocol version, request identity, requested operation, outcome, deepest validated stage, stage account, artifact identity and digest when validated, verification disposition when supplied, faults, and fixed non-authority
  + is deterministic and normalized for equal requests
  + response validity means coherent evidence replay only

& [CLI]
  + add a provider-free cantor-compiler-lab binary that reads one request from stdin or one explicitly named file and writes one response to stdout
  + stdout remains machine JSON; diagnostics go to stderr
  + exit 0 means structurally valid lifecycle evidence, exit 1 means semantic refusal, and exit 2 means input or invocation fault
  + the binary performs no writes, subprocess creation, network access, dependency fetch, signing, clock read, installation, deployment, artifact execution, or successor recognition

& [Acceptance]
  + exact complete artifact and verification fixtures validate through both library and CLI
  + tampered forms fail at their earliest dependency boundary with a typed fault
  + malformed, trailing, unknown-field, oversized, wrong-version, mismatched-operation, and incomplete-stage inputs refuse
  + validation response cannot be presented as build authorization, execution evidence, verification passage, or global single-use consumption
  + focused debug, optimized release, complete workspace, warnings-denied lint, format, evidence, and diff gates pass

& [Locked]
  + production build runner, filesystem mutation, global attempt-ledger CAS, secret keys, signing, network, clock, install, deploy, execute, admit, self-replace, internal llama.cpp, FPGA, remote machines, OneDrive, EVO-X2, and Minecraft
